{
  "slug": "nerdygeek",
  "name": "Nerdygeek",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "NerdyGeek gives Claude Code a version-aware documentation lookup tool that dynamically discovers official docs for frameworks and libraries, retrieves the most relevant sections, filters noise, and returns structured answers with source links and code examples. It is designed to help coding agents recover from uncertainty quickly and continue working with current documentation instead of stale assumptions.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `latest-docs` (Fetch live, version-aware official documentation for any language, framework, or library) and **1 MCP server**, `nerdygeek`.\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install nerdygeek@claude-community` from `docxbox/NerdyGeek`.\n\nNerdyGeek is an open-source TypeScript Node.js MCP server and Claude Code plugin that helps coding agents stop guessing from stale memory.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
